ecides to teach him the  tricks of the trade behind his  employer's backs turns out steve is a  very good learner so much so that bishop  may not only have his bosses to worry  about frequent bronson collaborator  michael winner directs this surprisingly  nuanced take on the business of death  bronson shares the screen with his  real-life wife joe ireland 70s  heartthrob jan michael vincent and dr  strangelove star keenan nguyen the  mechanic was remade in 2011 with jason  statham and ben foster and the bishop  and steve rose respectively and was  successful enough to yield a sequel  mechanic resurrection in 2016. it's hard  to beat the original though for both its  portrayal of the mechanics of  assassination and the humanity of its  characters  before spy kids and elita writer  director robert rodriguez began his  career with el mariachi starring carlos  gallardo as a particularly unlucky  traveling musician who finds himself a  victim of mistaken identity arriving in  a new town with nothing but his guitar  el mariachi isn't looking for trouble  however he finds it when the notorious  killer azul known for his guitar case  full of guns escapes from jail raising  the ire of the drug kingpin moko  unfortunately for el mariachi the hitman  moko sends after azul can't tell the  difference between the criminal and the  performer and chaos ensues even when el  mariachi finally manages to escape the  action he finds himself roped right back  into it after falling in love with  moko's love interest domino gallardo  stars alongside consuelo gomez reynold  martinez and peter marquardt who all  give enduring performances rodriguez's  kinetic style and flair for the dramatic  propelled this tragic tale of a man who  wanted nothing more than to be a  musician only to have his dream  shattered in the most painful way  the spanish language el mariachi was  made with no second takes on an ultra  low budget of just seven thousand  dollars the film's two sequels 1995's  desperado 