ken are in hiding because rey  recently botched a hit accidentally  killing a child and harry is absolutely  livid about it after all killing a child  violates the hitman's cold as rey and  can cool their hills in bruges belgium  harry tasks ken with taking care of rey  but ken's not too keen on that plan  harry doesn't appreciate ken's  disobedience so he heads to bruges  himself to get his hands dirty it's only  a matter of time before things come to a  bloody head in bruges finds a lot of  humor in a lot of places from a colorful  cast of supporting characters to the  profanity-laden tirades from its leads  farrell and gleason have excellent  chemistry constantly playing their  characters new roses off of each other  mcdonough also responsible for 2012's  seven psychopaths in 2017's three  billboards outside ebbing missouri  teases non-stop laughs out of a bleak  predicament infusing the story of a  bunch of killers and re-probates with  plenty of well-earned heart  the assassination bureau limited given  the snappier title of the assassination  bureau in the states also takes a darkly  comedic look at the hitman business but  without all the bleakness of inbruge  based on an unfinished novel by jack  london this 1969 picture stars oliver  reed as ivan dragamilov diana rigg as  sonja winter and telly savalas as lord  boswick winter is a journalist and  women's rights activist who discovers a  secret organization of assassins aptly  titled the assassination bureau limited  instead of exposing them in her capacity  as a journalist winter decides to have  the head of the bureau dragomilov killed  believing that a power vacuum would  dismantle the entire enterprise from the  top down she does this by soliciting a  hit on dragomilov from his own agency a  request that dragamilov surprisingly  accepts there's other conspiracies at  play however as newspaper baron lord  boswick has his own sinister plans to  take over the bureau the whole thing is  intentionally ridiculous and overly  complicated but a very fun watch  nonetheless  the second take on the hitman genre from  luke baison leon the professional was  originally released in 1994 as just the  professional in the u.s this time jean  renaud takes center stage as leon the  titular professional killer who finds  himself the guardian of 12 year old  matilda played by natalie portman it  hasn't exactly aged the best with  certain scenes ranging from problematic  to downright creepy but the film is  worth checking out for its explosive  action scenes and compelling revenge  narrative matilda and a family live in  the same apartment complex where leon  resides when matilda's drug-dealing  father runs afoul of gary oldman's loose  cannon dea agent norman stansfield  matilda returns home one day to find her  parents and siblings slaughtered in a  violent raid leon takes matilda in and  when she learns the truth about what he  does for a living she convinces him to  teach her the tricks of the murder trade  so she can avenge her four-year-old  brother over time leon and matilda form  an odd bond he teaches her weaponry and  tactics while she plots to take on  stansfield all by herself portman is a  tiny powerhouse of emotion and her debut  performance is a taste of what was to  come later on in her career renault is  also quite good at being a likable  killer and oldman often seems like he's  in a different movie from everyone else  entirely but in the best possible  way bring me everyone  what do you mean everyone everyone  matilda isn't the only adolescent  assassin on this list in 2011 circa  ronan played the title role in hannah  about a 15 year old girl whose father  teaches her the ways of the hitman  hannah's father eric an xcia operator  played by eric banner is being hunted by  his former employer because he knows too  much to protect his daughter eric does  what any loving father would do he  starts training her how to kill while  she's still in diapers he has motors of  his own however as he sends her off to  kill kate blanchett's cia agent marissa  wagler who's been sent to clean up  eric's loose ends hannah twists and  turns as the young assassin undertakes  her mission and discovers a dark secret  her father has been hiding from her for  her entire life hannah marries action  with coming-of-age drama with ronan  showing off the skill that had already  earned her an oscar nomination for best  supporting actress several years prior  director joe wright keeps the tension up  and the pacing tight as hannah heads  straight into a reveal that will turn  her entire world upside down a tv series  based on the film also called hannah per  made on amazon prime in 2019  john woo's groundbreaking 1986 hong kong  action film a better tomorrow is widely  considered the film that turned chao yun  fat into a superstar in asia chow plays  mark a high-ranking member of the  criminal triad alongside his friend  seung se ho played by t long things are  going great but there's a problem hole's  brother kit is a cop hell-bent on  stopping the triad hole wants to go  straight but as is always the case  during that one last job things get out  of control and he's sent to prison when  he's finally released after three years  ho discovers that his gang has had a  change in management his former  apprentice shang has usurped mark as the  boss  wu minds the tension between ho's  dedication to his brother and his  allegiance to his best friend while  meditating on what makes a family albeit  with a healthy dose of his trademark  bloodshed the relationships between hog  hit and mark make up the emotional heart  of the film a sequel a better tomorrow 2  was released in 1987 and a prequel a  better tomorrow 3 love and death in  saigon in 1989. the latter was directed  by troy hark after he and wu had a  falling out a better tomorrow has also  gotten its fair share of remakes with a  1994 hindi version called atish a 2010  korean version and a 2018 chinese remake  a better tomorrow 2018. check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  films are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]

