ous and overly  complicated but a very fun watch  nonetheless  the second take on the hitman genre from  luke baison leon the professional was  originally released in 1994 as just the  professional in the u.s this time jean  renaud takes center stage as leon the  titular professional killer who finds  himself the guardian of 12 year old  matilda played by natalie portman it  hasn't exactly aged the best with  certain scenes ranging from problematic  to downright creepy but the film is  worth checking out for its explosive  action scenes and compelling revenge  narrative matilda and a family live in  the same apartment complex where leon  resides when matilda's drug-dealing  father runs afoul of gary oldman's loose  cannon dea agent norman stansfield  matilda returns home one day to find her  parents and siblings slaughtered in a  violent raid leon takes matilda in and  when she learns the truth about what he  does for a living she convinces him to  teach her the tricks of the murder trade  so she can avenge her four-year-old  brother over time leon and matilda form  an odd bond he teaches her weaponry and  tactics while she plots to take on  stansfield all by herself portman is a  tiny powerhouse of emotion and her debut  performance is a taste of what was to  come later on in her career renault is  also quite good at being a likable  killer and oldman often seems like he's  in a different movie from everyone else  entirely but in the best possible  way bring me everyone  what do you mean everyone everyone  matilda isn't the only adolescent  assassin on this list in 2011 circa  ronan played the title role in hannah  about a 15 year old girl whose father  teaches her the ways of the hitman  hannah's father eric an xcia operator  played by eric banner is being hunted by  his former employer because he knows too  much to protect his daughter eric does  what any loving father would do he  starts training her how to kill while  she's still in diapers he has motors of  his own however as he sends her off to  kill kate blanchett's cia agent marissa  wagler who's been sent to clean up  eric's loose ends hannah twists and  turns as the young assassin undertakes  her mission and discovers a dark secret  her father has been hiding from her for  her entire life hannah marries action  with coming-of-age drama with ronan  showing off the skill that had already  earned her an oscar nomination for best  supporting actress several years prior  director joe wright keeps the tension up  and the pacing tight as hannah heads  straight into a reveal that will turn  her entire world upside down a tv series  based on the film also called hannah per  made on amazon prime in 2019  john woo's groundbreaking 1986 hong kong  action film a better tomorrow is widely  considered the film that turned chao yun  fat into a superstar in asia chow plays  mark a high-ranking member of the  criminal triad alongside his friend  seung se ho played by t long things are  going great but there's a problem hole's  brother kit is a cop hell-bent on  stopping the triad hole wants to go  straight but as is always the case  during that one last job things get out  of control and he's sent to prison when  he's finally released after three years  ho discovers that his gang has had a  change in management his former  apprentice shang has usurped mark as the  boss  wu minds the tension between ho's  dedication to his brother and his  allegiance to his best friend while  meditating on what makes a family albeit  with a healthy dose of his trademark  bloodshed the relationships between hog  hit and mark make up the emotional heart  of the film a sequel a better tomorrow 2  was released in 1987 and a prequel a  better tomorrow 3 love and death in  saigon in 1989. the latter was directed  by troy hark after he and wu had a  falling out a better tomorrow has also  gotten its fair share of remakes with a  1994 hindi version called atish a 2010  korean version and a 2018 chinese remake  a better tomorrow 2018. check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  films are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

